          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.102,
            0.869,
            0.151
          ],
          "content": "**15. Two lamps, one rated 100 W at 220 V, and the other 60 W at 220 V, are connected in parallel to electric mains supply. What current is drawn from the line if the supply voltage is 220 V?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.154,
            0.868,
            0.172
          ],
          "content": "**16. Which uses more energy, a 250 W TV set in 1 hr, or a 1200 W toaster in 10 minutes?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.174,
            0.867,
            0.208
          ],
          "content": "**17. An electric heater of resistance 44** Ω **draws 5 A from the service mains for 2 hours. Calculate the rate at which heat is developed in the heater.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.21,
            0.349,
            0.228
          ],
          "content": "**18. Explain the following.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.23,
            0.857,
            0.248
          ],
          "content": "**(a) Why is the tungsten used almost exclusively for filament of electric lamps?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.249,
            0.868,
            0.284
          ],
          "content": "**(b) Why are the conductors of electric heating devices, such as bread-toasters and electric irons, made of an alloy rather than a pure metal?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.286,
            0.748,
            0.304
          ],
          "content": "**(c) Why is the series arrangement not used for domestic circuits?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.306,
            0.803,
            0.323
          ],
          "content": "**(d) How does the resistance of a wire vary with its area of cross-section?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.326,
            0.869,
            0.359
          ],
          "content": "**(e) Why are copper and aluminium wires usually employed for electricity transmission?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.092,
